1..12
ok 1 a descoped AC stops blocking and the gate passes a genuinely finished thread
ok 2 off-scope ACs are reported separately, never folded away
ok 3 the audit trail lands on the line, which is the whole point over deleting it
ok 4 a descope names a real thread, never itself, and never nothing
ok 5 a withdrawal without a stated reason is refused
ok 6 rescope and reinstate undo their own state and refuse the other's
ok 7 an off-scope AC is not re-entered by another off-scope verb
ok 8 a descoped test-backed AC is off-scope before it is hunted for a covering AT
ok 9 an off-scope AC cannot be satisfied, and the refusal names the undo
ok 10 a contract emptied by off-scope moves is refused, not passed on an empty set
ok 11 a field value carrying the delimiter is refused rather than mangled
ok 12 satisfied: n/a is read as itself, not as a truncated token
